  "help": {
    "title": "Frequently Asked Questions",
    "q1": "How do I clock in correctly?",
    "a1": "You need to clock in during your assigned shift using the 'Clock In' button or use the biometric attendance machine at the office.",
    "q2": "What should I do if I forget to clock in?",
    "a2": "Submit an attendance adjustment request or inform your direct manager for confirmation.",
    "q3": "How can I contact technical support?",
    "a3": "Send an email to the IT department or call the internal hotline 1234 during working hours.",
    "q4": "Can incorrect attendance records be corrected?",
    "a4": "Yes. You can submit a correction request with a reason, and your manager will review it.",
    "q5": "When is overtime counted?",
    "a5": "Overtime is valid only when pre-approved by the manager and when you clock out after regular working hours.",
    "q6": "When is salary calculated and paid?",
    "a6": "Salary is calculated from the 21st to the 20th of each month and paid on the 25th.",
    "q7": "Where can I check the details if my salary is lower than expected?",
    "a7": "You can view deduction details in the 'Payroll' section. If something seems incorrect, contact the HR department.",
    "q8": "When do employees become eligible for official employment?",
    "a8": "The probation period is 2 months. After meeting the requirements, the official contract will be issued within 5 days.",
    "q9": "When will my employment contract be renewed?",
    "a9": "Thirty days before the contract expires, the system sends a reminder and HR will contact you for renewal.",
    "q10": "When does the company start paying insurance for employees?",
    "a10": "The company pays social, health, and unemployment insurance from the month following the official contract date.",
    "q11": "How is annual leave calculated?",
    "a11": "Employees receive 12 days of annual leave per year plus one extra day for each year of seniority.",
    "q12": "How do I register for a training course?",
    "a12": "You can register in the 'Training' section. Mandatory courses will automatically be assigned to you.",
    "q13": "How can I update my personal information?",
    "a13": "Go to the 'Personal Profile' section, update the information, and submit for HR approval if required."
  }
}